Source: ironbar
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: AI-agent <noreply@example.com>
# Not packaged in Debian (neither trixie nor sid), so the debian/ directory is
# written from scratch by upstream sources:
#   * no -doc/-examples/-tests stanza; documentation is not built (cargo build),
#     no man pages, no debian/tests directory;
#   * X11 is not used: it is a Wayland GTK4 Layer Shell bar, built against the
#     GTK 4 of this repository;
#   * dbgsym packages are not built (general rule in scripts/build-package.sh);
#   * cargo builds fetch crates from crates.io at build time (network required),
#     versions pinned by Cargo.lock shipped in the tarball.
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 dh-cargo,
 libdbus-1-dev,
 libgit2-dev,
 libgtk-4-dev,
 libgtk4-layer-shell-dev,
 libinput-dev,
 libluajit-5.1-dev,
 libpulse-dev,
 libssl-dev,
 pkgconf,
 rustc,
 cargo,
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Homepage: https://github.com/JakeStanger/ironbar
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/JakeStanger/ironbar
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/JakeStanger/ironbar.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ironbar
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: customisable GTK4 Layer Shell bar for Wayland compositors
 Ironbar is a customisable and feature-rich GTK4 bar for Wayland compositors,
 written in Rust. It supports Sway, Hyprland and Niri, and provides modules
 for clock, tray, volume, network, music, workspaces and more.
